sheet order (reverse of dependency order) = Out, Mid, Inputs, Cycle, Cycle2
Inputs A1 = 10
Mid    A1 = 20   (Inputs!A1*2)
Out    A1 = 21   (Mid!A1+1)

== recalculating ONE sheet is not enough, and says so by being wrong ==
after recalc(wb, "Out") : Out A1 = 21   (stale; correct is 201)

== recalculating the WORKBOOK orders across sheets ==
evaluated = 4
changed   = 4
circular  = 2
Mid A1 = 200   (Inputs!A1*2)
Out A1 = 201   (transitive: needed the NEW Mid)
Out B1 = 305   (SUM(Mid!A1:A2)+Inputs!A1)

== a cycle ACROSS sheets is reported, not iterated ==
Cycle  B1 (healthy neighbour) = 300

== the new values persist, and the formulas survive ==
Out A1 value   = 201
Out A1 formula = Mid!A1+1
Mid A1 value   = 200
Mid A1 formula = Inputs!A1*2
